      "body": "## Summary\n\nFrom verified replica journal to offline spectator service:\n\n`DurableReceiver` → non-mutating parse/restore → directory-aware capability authorization → program reconstruction/Records → read-only `WorldHandle` → existing world session protocol.\n\n- Phase 3 PR #4634 is merged at `844fac4c333baaeb5e5871298bedaa4beb095b69`.\n- Replica restore preserves journaled presence without synthesizing leave events; only JOIN is effective on replicas.\n- The actor refuses local mutations, events, schedules, ticks, program capability effects, and journal writes. Replica opens replay directory and artifact sidecars without repairing them.\n- No CLI/configuration or offline admission policy is added; phase 5 task 6699 owns authenticated sidecar refresh and Drew's explicit decision.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- **Before:** no replica open/serve path; the durable receiver only persisted and verified journal bytes.\n- **After:** `cargo test --lib replica` — 51 passed; `cargo test --lib read_only_` — 4 passed. Includes friend-delegated authorization with no writer actor, nested-group/old-directory replay, checkpoint refusal, the existing session protocol, mutation refusal, offline module restore and Records parity, and unchanged sidecars. Existing friend-delegation and session-contract tests also pass.\n- **CI coverage:** current `id-check.yml` lacks a `pull_request` trigger (tracked in #3045). Manually dispatched on the current head as run [41564760029](https://github.com/developing-today/code/actions/runs/41564760029); results pending.\n\n## Merge Danger\n\n**Door:** two-way.\n\n**Blast Radius:** moderate — world restore, session authorization, and the replica-only actor mode. The writer path remains unchanged by default.",
